From d382e57cdc7f6df23438755453cd4071810f38a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rv-rocm <rv-rocm@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:20:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] riscv64/gfx1201 adaptations for PyTorch v2.13.0 (TheRock 10.0
 dist)

Full working-tree adaptation delta vs tag v2.13.0 (134 files):
- torch/csrc (128 files): 7.1.1-style mechanical HIP adaptation
  (c10/cuda -> c10/hip header swaps, CUDA/HIP guards) required to
  compile against ROCm/HIP on riscv64
- mha_all_aot.hip: fix DeviceIndex narrowing (clang23 rejects
  braced-init (char) casts) at 3 sites
- LoadHIP.cmake / Dependencies.cmake / ATen CMakeLists: TheRock 10.0
  dist paths, gfx1201 target, hipify invocation
- CUDAHooks.cpp / python_variable_methods.cpp: riscv64 guards
Builds clean against TheRock 10.0 dist (HIP 7.15.26366, clang 23.0.0git).
Wheel verified on R9700: GPU matmul OK; vLLM benchmark 3454 tok/s total.

